    `Father, I come today to the Person I have most consistently neglected in my trinitarian faith — the Holy Spirit, who lives in me, who was sent to be my Paraclete, who guides into all truth and speaks what He hears from You and tells of what is to come. I receive today the fellowship — the koinonia — that 2 Corinthians 13:14 describes. Not access to a power. Communion with a Person. Teach me to keep in step with Him the way Galatians 5:25 describes — matching my pace and direction to His, not dragging behind and not running past, but walking together in the genuine alignment of two people who are genuinely going the same direction. Develop in me the sensitivity to hear His voice in the ordinary moments — the nudge, the prompting, the conviction that arrives quietly rather than dramatically. Holy Spirit, I acknowledge You today as a Person. I am listening. Guide me into the truth You have for today.`
